# Yasharn, Implacable Earth's ban is judged as the cost is paid (CR 601.2h by way of 602.2b), not only as the ability is
# begun. Bot2's Yasharn has lost all its abilities to Bot1's The Wondrous Wasp ("for as long as The Wondrous Wasp remains
# on the battlefield"), so Bot1's Ornithopter, equipped with Deconstruction Hammer, may begin "{3}, {T}, Sacrifice
# Deconstruction Hammer" at Bot2's Sol Ring. Bot1 pays the {3} with Ashnod's Altar, sacrificing the Wasp, and a Mox Pearl:
# with the Wasp gone Yasharn has its ability again, the Hammer can't be sacrificed, and the activation is taken back
# (CR 601.2h: unpayable costs can't be paid; CR 733.1). The Hammer stays, the Ornithopter untapped, and the Sol Ring
# survives: the Wasp's effect ends as the Wasp leaves (CR 611.2b), not at the next state-based check.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Deconstruction Hammer
Ashnod's Altar
The Wondrous Wasp
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Yasharn, Implacable Earth
Island
Sol Ring
Island x16

